# web.config was ignored until 2026-08-21. It is tracked now, on the dev's call, because this
# effort puts real changes in it - the "static file 404 without booting PHP" rewrite rule and the
# <location path="build/assets"> cache rule - and an untracked file means every server has to be
# edited by hand with nothing to diff against.
#
# CARE ON THE FIRST DEPLOY: the production server has its own web.config that has never been in
# git. Compare the two before you let a deploy overwrite it. See DEPLOYMENT.md section 7.
# web.config
# Vite writes a throwaway vite.config.<ext>.timestamp-*.mjs next to the config
# while loading it. Ignore only those. A blanket `*.mjs` used to sit here and it
# is what kept the root vite config out of git entirely.
/vite.config.*.timestamp-*.mjs
/plans
database/phase1_migrations.sql
/bootstrap/cache
.claude/launch.json
